check('mle.training_memory_diagnosis','Diagnostics save each loss tensor with its graph even though no future derivative through the saved values is needed. Which isolated change addresses this evidence?', 'Save scalar or detached diagnostic values instead, then rerun the same bounded workload and compare measured peaks.', 'Call empty_cache while retaining all graph-connected losses and claim live tensors were freed.', 'empty_cache cannot release storage still occupied by live tensors.', 'Keep the graph-connected losses and relabel reserved memory as unused tensor-free memory.', 'Reserved and allocated quantities are distinct; relabeling does not remove live graph references.', 'Ask whether the diagnostic really needs a gradient connection.')
